      "slug": "our-craft",
      "title": "The Artisanal Weaves of AABHA",
      "subtitle": "Preserving handloom craftsmanship across Rajasthan & Bengal",
      "heroImage": "/images/brand_story_editorial_1791119191742.jpg",
      "content": "Each garment at AABHA is conceived as a living homage to indigenous Indian textile art. From hand-spun Chanderi silk to delicate Mulmul cotton, our karigars spend weeks perfecting each silhouette.\n\nWe employ pure French seams, hand-rolled hems, and skin-friendly natural dyes so that every piece feels effortless against your skin from morning celebrations to midnight soirees.",
      "published": true,
      "metaTitle": "Our Craft & Heritage | AABHA CLOTHING",
      "metaDescription": "Discover the artisanal craftsmanship and handloom heritage behind AABHA ethnic wear.",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-01",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-22"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-garment-care",
      "slug": "garment-care",
      "title": "Garment Longevity & Mulmul Care Guide",
      "subtitle": "Nurturing your handloom ensembles for years of grace",
      "heroImage": "/images/hero_slide_ethnic_1791228741882.jpg",
      "content": "Natural fibers like Mulmul, Chanderi, and organza are delicate treasures. We recommend gentle hand-washing in cold water with mild organic detergent, or professional dry cleaning for embroidered and zari garments.\n\nAlways air dry in shade to preserve color brilliance, and iron inside out on a low-to-medium silk setting.",
      "published": true,
      "metaTitle": "Garment Care & Longevity Guide | AABHA CLOTHING",
      "metaDescription": "Best practices for caring for your hand-spun Chanderi, Mulmul, and artisanal ensembles.",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-01",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-22"
    }
